{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_nexus_ecs", "label": "Nexus ECS (@atlasjs/nexus)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/nexus-ecs.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sparse-set ECS consumed by @atlasjs/gameplay; the refactor targeted one correctness bug already firing in prod, an entity-recycling time bomb, and a double indirection in the hot path."}, {"id": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_entity_generations", "label": "Generational entities", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/nexus-ecs.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Multiplicative index+generation packing (21-bit index) avoids BigInt on the hot path; stale handles now fail cleanly instead of silently applying to a recycled id (ABA)."}, {"id": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_icomponentstore", "label": "IComponentStore seam", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/nexus-ecs.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Makes a future SoA/archetype migration painless: systems never see this interface, they only see query, so the backend can be swapped without touching gameplay."}, {"id": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_sparsesetstore", "label": "SparseSetStore", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/nexus-ecs.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sparse indexed by entityIndex (compact, bounded by peak live entities) while dense stores the full packed Entity, so dense[i] === entity also rejects stale handles."}, {"id": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_typed_query", "label": "Typed query with each()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/nexus-ecs.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The query already holds the stores, so handing components straight to the callback removes the per-entity requireComponent re-lookup and array allocation; args array is reused and applied, never spread."}, {"id": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_fail_fast_guard", "label": "Fail-fast structural-change guard", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/nexus-ecs.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Version is checked BEFORE the bound test each iteration \u2014 otherwise a swap-remove shrinking size below the current index exits the loop before re-checking, silently skipping entities at counts of 1-2."}, {"id": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_command_buffer", "label": "Hybrid command buffer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/nexus-ecs.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "EnTT/flecs model: direct mutation by default, deferred via world.commands when mutating during a query. spawn() stays immediate because creating a bare entity touches no component store."}, {"id": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_hybrid_flush", "label": "Auto-flush at lane Sync", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/nexus-ecs.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "NexusPlugin registers a nexus:flush step in the trailing Sync stage of all three lanes, so every plugin using the world gets flushing for free without wiring it."}, {"id": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_multi_world", "label": "Multi-world isolation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/nexus-ecs.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_componentregistry", "label": "ComponentRegistry", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/nexus-ecs.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Replaces mutable module-global state and the ctor monkeypatch; a shared default registry keeps ids stable across worlds while injecting a fresh one gives total isolation for tests/hot-reload."}, {"id": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_query_filters", "label": "without / optional query filters", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/nexus-ecs.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Immutable builder resolving extra stores through a StoreResolver so the query never depends on the concrete world; optional() does not affect membership, only widens the tuple with |undefined."}, {"id": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_lifecycle_events", "label": "world.onAdd / world.onRemove", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/nexus-ecs.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Mediated by the world rather than the store so IComponentStore stays unchanged; this is the brick that lets external entity-keyed storages (runtimeBodiesStorage) be cleaned automatically."}, {"id": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_structural_mutation_bug", "label": "Structural mutation during iteration bug", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/nexus-ecs.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Live-array iteration plus swap-remove made TransformWriteRequestCleanupSystem skip every other entity, so cleanup only partially drained each frame \u2014 the original motivation for the guard and the command buffer."}, {"id": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_perf_target", "label": "Perf target 1k\u20133k entities @ 60fps", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/core/nexus-ecs.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "At this scale pointer chasing and GC of class instances are negligible, so SoA/archetype would be engineering paid in DX with no visible gain; safety comes from the abstraction, not the representation."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_nexus_ecs", "target": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_entity_generations", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/core/nexus-ecs.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_nexus_ecs", "target": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_icomponentstore", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/core/nexus-ecs.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_nexus_ecs", "target": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_typed_query", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/core/nexus-ecs.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_nexus_ecs", "target": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_command_buffer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/core/nexus-ecs.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_nexus_ecs", "target": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_multi_world", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/core/nexus-ecs.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_nexus_ecs", "target": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_query_filters", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/core/nexus-ecs.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_nexus_ecs", "target": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_lifecycle_events", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/core/nexus-ecs.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_ne